## Typescript inference of query results
Ideally, fetchAllPaginatedResults should introspect the query being passed to it and annotate the returned type accordingly, to avoid missing types or having to duplicate them.

```
fetchAllPaginatedResults
```


```
// the ideal scenario: automatic type inference

const { data } = await fetchAllPaginatedResults(
  adminClient.from('assets').select('*', { count: 'exact' }),
)
// ^? data: AssetRow[] | null
```


```
// the ideal scenario: automatic type inference

const { data } = await fetchAllPaginatedResults(
  adminClient.from('assets').select('*', { count: 'exact' }),
)
// ^? data: AssetRow[] | null
```

We can leverage [Typescript generics](https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/generics.html) to do so, adding a variable to fetchAllPaginatedResults, which TS will match to the parameters being sent to the function:

```
fetchAllPaginatedResults
```


```
export async function fetchAllPaginatedResults<
  QueryBuilder extends PostgrestFilterBuilder<any, any, any>,
>(
  queryBuilder: QueryBuilder,
  accumulator?: {
    data: Awaited<QueryBuilder>['data']
    count?: number | null
    fromRange: number
  },
) {
	// ... function body
}
```


